-bin/catalog-gen turns that into catalog/catalog-info.yaml with its dependsOn edges. This
-file is the third renderer of the same inventory: it reads the catalogue and writes one
-Mermaid page. It collects nothing, so it can never disagree with the catalogue.
-
-    estate-diagram                      render catalog/catalog-info.yaml -> docs/architecture/live.md
-    estate-diagram --catalog F --out G  other paths (the tests use a fixture)
-    estate-diagram --check              exit 1 when the page on disk is not what the catalogue says
