-# Chaos Mesh cannot pass the estate's restricted policy set, by design: chaos-daemon reaches
-# into the container runtime (hostPID, a hostPath to the containerd socket, privileged, extra
-# capabilities) to inject the faults ADR 0005 chose it for. Incident 2026-08-26: idp#139
-# installed the HelmRelease and Kyverno refused chaos-daemon and chaos-controller-manager
-# (22 rule failures across 13 policies, kyverno CLI 1.19.0 against the prospector policy set); the chaos-mesh row
-# stalled and no pod ever ran.
-#
-# The exception is Kyverno's own mechanism for this (kyverno.io/docs/writing-policies/exceptions)
-# and is scoped to one namespace, so nothing outside chaos-mesh is loosened: the same object
-# with another namespace still refuses all 22 (tests/test_incident_chaos_mesh_refused_by_kyverno.py).
-# Only the policies the rendered chart fails are listed; the incident test refuses a waiver
-# for a policy the chart already passes.
-# It lives in namespace kyverno because platform/edge/kyverno.yaml restricts exceptions to that
-# namespace; an exception a workload namespace could write for itself would not be a guard.
-apiVersion: kyverno.io/v2
-kind: PolicyException
-metadata:
-  name: chaos-mesh
-  namespace: kyverno
-spec:
-  match:
-    any:
-      - resources:
-          namespaces:
-            - chaos-mesh
-          kinds:
-            - Pod
-            - DaemonSet
-            - Deployment
-            - ReplicaSet
-  exceptions:
-    - policyName: disallow-capabilities
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: disallow-capabilities-strict
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: disallow-host-namespaces
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: disallow-host-path
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: disallow-privilege-escalation
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: disallow-privileged-containers
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: drop-all-capabilities
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: require-pod-probes
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: require-requests-limits
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: require-ro-rootfs
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: require-run-as-nonroot
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: restrict-seccomp-strict
-      ruleNames: ['*']
-    - policyName: restrict-volume-types
-      ruleNames: ['*']
