-# SigNoz on the one 1.8-core / 9.2 GiB OKE node (crew#258 CP2). Requests are sized so the node
-# stays under its allocatable CPU: 1270m was requested before this release (kubectl describe node,
-# 2026-08-25). Kyverno enforces the restricted profile, so every pod carries limits, probes,
-# non-root, seccomp and a read-only root filesystem with emptyDir scratch where the process writes.
